<div class="sample" aria-label="An example entry and the letter that answers it">
  <blockquote class="entry">
    <b>Your entry, Tuesday evening</b>
    Spent the whole day at my desk and got nothing done. I keep opening the same document and closing it again.
  </blockquote>
  <article class="letter">
    <header>
      <h2>A letter from Seneca</h2>
      <time datetime="2026-10-20T21:14">Tue, 20 Oct 2026 · 21:14</time>
    </header>
    <p>My friend,</p>
    <p>You write that the day felt wasted, that you sat at your desk and nothing moved. Yet you noticed it, and noticing is the first step back to yourself. Most people let such days pass without a glance.</p>
    <div class="question">
      <span class="label">A question to sit with</span>
      <p>What would you do with one hour if no one could see the result?</p>
    </div>
    <p>Tomorrow, guard one hour as if it were the only one you owned.</p>
    <p class="sign">Yours, Seneca</p>
  </article>
</div>

<section class="block" aria-labelledby="how">
  <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><div><h3>Write your entry</h3><p>A few lines or a few pages. Add how you feel today.</p></div></li>
    <li><div><h3>Choose who reads it</h3><p>Pick a mentor, or Future You, the person you are becoming.</p></div></li>
    <li><div><h3>Get a letter back</h3><p>A personal reply in their voice. Answer it and the conversation continues.</p></div></li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="block" aria-labelledby="mentors">
